{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB14031 - MONDO_3582",
  "verbalization": "Tretamine is implicated in the treatment of malignant non-dysgerminomatous germ cell tumors of the ovary, which are associated with Hereditary Breast Ovarian Cancer Syndrome. This relationship is supported by the presence of Tretamine as an indication for multiple chemotherapy agents—Rucaparib, Melphalan, and Belotecan—each of which is linked to the syndrome. The shared indication for these agents suggests a potential mechanistic link between Tretamine and the syndrome, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence is strengthened by the presence of a common target or pathway in the context of these cancers, though no direct evidence of Tretamine's mode of action on the syndrome is provided. The integration of these paths highlights the possibility that Tretamine may influence pathways involved in the development or progression of Hereditary Breast Ovarian Cancer Syndrome, though further investigation is needed to confirm this hypothesis.",
